== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Consciousness-Responsive Metamaterials ===

The highest-level Track B speculation: if biological cortical tissue has a state-dependent <math>\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}(t)</math>, and if the [[Psi Stabilizer]] shell is designed so that the operator's cortex occupies a significant volume fraction of the resonant cavity, then the effective medium of the cavity changes when the operator's coherence state changes. The cavity becomes a '''consciousness-responsive metamaterial''' — its ψ resonant properties are not fixed by the shell geometry alone but shift with the operator's attentional state.

In principle this would be visible as a shift in the cavity resonant frequency <math>\omega_{010}</math> correlated with RMSSD — without any change in the shell material or applied fields. If detected, this would be among the most direct evidence for the ψ hypothesis. If not detected (shell frequency independent of operator state after accounting for mechanical effects), it would constrain <math>|\Delta\chi_\psi^{\rm (bio)}| < 0.01</math> across HRV coherence states.

=== OSGS Mode Composition and Device Synthesis ===

Extending the primitive-to-mode correspondence into a compositional design calculus: given a desired ψ device function, decompose it into a sequence of mode operations (source, guide, convert, focus, filter, detect), map each operation to its primitive symbol via the correspondence table, and synthesise the composite symbol. The composite symbol specifies the metamaterial architecture as a sequence of TPMS unit cells of different topologies arranged in the required spatial order.

This would make ψ device design partially algorithmic: specify the function in symbolic terms, translate to a geometry specification, fabricate the TPMS sequence. The [[OSGS]] would function as a high-level design language for ψ metamaterials.

== TML Measurement Protocol ==

=== TML-1: Topology Discrimination Test ===

The primary test of ψ metamaterial design principles. Six samples, each implementing one OSGS primitive topology:

# Print six 10 mm × 10 mm × 10 mm samples using the B7+B8 protocol, each with a different unit cell geometry: (1) solid sphere inclusion, (2) linear channel, (3) toroidal channel, (4) standard Gyroid (Wave), (5) 45° angled junction, (6) graded-density hemisphere.
# Fill identically with B8 composite (same batch).
# Measure S11, S21 from 1 kHz to 1 MHz via VNA for each sample.
# Test: are the six S21 spectra statistically distinguishable? Compute Mahalanobis distance between spectra in the frequency-amplitude space.

'''Pass criterion:''' At least four of the six spectra are distinguishable at > 3σ significance from the mean of the remaining five. This constitutes evidence that topology — not just fill chemistry — determines ψ metamaterial properties.

=== TML-2: Graded-Index Focusing Verification ===

Print a graded-t TPMS hemisphere (Class II, Luneburg lens profile). Place a bifilar coil ψ source at one focus. Measure field amplitude with OPM probe at the predicted opposite focus. Compare against a uniform-t control (no focusing). Pass criterion: ≥ 2× field enhancement at focus relative to control.

=== TML-3: Consciousness-Responsive Frequency Shift ===

With full [[Psi Stabilizer]] shell assembled and operator present, measure shell resonant frequency shift between baseline and peak HRV coherence states. All mechanical and thermal confounds controlled via sham. Pass criterion: frequency shift > 3× measurement noise floor, correlated with RMSSD at r > 0.7.

